  "name": "EleutherIA",
  "description": "EleutherIA is an open scholarly research platform and FAIR-aligned knowledge graph for ancient debates on free will, fate, moral responsibility, and agency across the Greco-Roman and early Christian worlds. As of the 2026-03-10 audit bundled with this release, the live graph contains 17,396 nodes, 42,161 edges, and 13,293 passage citations; the broader platform indexes 487 ancient works and more than 69,000 passages in Greek, Latin, English, Hebrew, and Arabic.",
